timestamp of the last sample, the metric name is dropped
tags	timestamp	value
Array(Tuple(String, String))	DateTime64(3)	Float64
[('job','a')]	1970-01-01 00:03:20.000	180
offset and @ select an older sample, its own timestamp is returned
[('job','a')]	120
[('job','a')]	60.5
any other expression returns the evaluation time
[('job','a')]	200.25
range query
[('job','a')]	[(100000,60.5),(150000,120),(200000,180)]
[('job','a')]	[(150000,60.5),(200000,120)]
[('job','a')]	[(100000,60.5),(150000,60.5),(200000,60.5)]
[('job','a')]	[(100000,100),(150000,150),(200000,200)]
a stale marker hides the series as it does for the selector itself
[('job','b')]	100
[('job','b')]	[(100000,100)]
Float32 values do not affect the precision of the timestamps
tags	timestamp	value
Array(Tuple(String, String))	DateTime64(3, \'UTC\')	Float64
[('job','j')]	2025-11-30 10:30:10.000	1764498605.125
